{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00412",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 1.28,
      "end_seconds": 5.3,
      "duration_seconds": 4.02,
      "text": "Morning, doctor. I've settled them in, ready when you are."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 8.24,
      "end_seconds": 11.54,
      "duration_seconds": 3.3,
      "text": "Thank you. Good morning, tell me what's been going on."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 12.2,
      "end_seconds": 24.13,
      "duration_seconds": 11.93,
      "text": "I mean, you know, so the thing is, I've got a very painful, swollen big toe. I kept putting it off, which I know isn't sensible."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 24.39,
      "end_seconds": 26.27,
      "duration_seconds": 1.88,
      "text": "Okay. How often does it happen?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 27.78,
      "end_seconds": 29.57,
      "duration_seconds": 1.79,
      "text": "Honestly, all the time."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 30.14,
      "end_seconds": 32.91,
      "duration_seconds": 2.77,
      "text": "On a normal day, how strong is it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 33.66,
      "end_seconds": 40.03,
      "duration_seconds": 6.37,
      "text": "Moderate, I'd say. I had warmth in the toe before. That's settled now, though."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 40.94,
      "end_seconds": 43.53,
      "duration_seconds": 2.59,
      "text": "Has anything about your daily routine changed lately?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 43.86,
      "end_seconds": 59.96,
      "duration_seconds": 16.1,
      "text": "Not really, the days are pretty much the same, work and home, and I've been trying to fit appointments in around my schedule, which isn't always easy, so I'm glad we could find a time today."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 62.49,
      "end_seconds": 64.32,
      "duration_seconds": 1.83,
      "text": "Any recent illness or rash?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 65.89,
      "end_seconds": 70.82,
      "duration_seconds": 4.93,
      "text": "Hmm, um, no, no recent illness or rash."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 73.51,
      "end_seconds": 75.08,
      "duration_seconds": 1.57,
      "text": "Anything unusual with passing urine?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 76.59,
      "end_seconds": 78.02,
      "duration_seconds": 1.43,
      "text": "Nothing there, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 79.45,
      "end_seconds": 82.96,
      "duration_seconds": 3.51,
      "text": "Do you need me to explain anything as we go?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 84.1,
      "end_seconds": 91.16,
      "duration_seconds": 7.06,
      "text": "Yeah, you know, just tell me in plain language, please. I'm not good with the medical terms."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 91.97,
      "end_seconds": 98.08,
      "duration_seconds": 6.11,
      "text": "Do you have any medical conditions, anything you've been treated for? I'll explain everything as we go along."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 98.88,
      "end_seconds": 105.39,
      "duration_seconds": 6.51,
      "text": "I've got high blood pressure. I thought it would sort itself out, but it hasn't."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 106.4,
      "end_seconds": 113.94,
      "duration_seconds": 7.54,
      "text": "Alright. Right, so that's your known high blood pressure. We'll keep that in mind today. How's everything else at home otherwise?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 115.48,
      "end_seconds": 122.27,
      "duration_seconds": 6.79,
      "text": "Busy. Everyone's running in different directions at the moment, you know how it is."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 123.69,
      "end_seconds": 126.96,
      "duration_seconds": 3.27,
      "text": "Any medication at the moment, including things from the pharmacy?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 127.48,
      "end_seconds": 130.8,
      "duration_seconds": 3.32,
      "text": "Ramipril. I take it 5 milligrams, every morning."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 131.22,
      "end_seconds": 133.47,
      "duration_seconds": 2.25,
      "text": "How long have you been on it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 134.77,
      "end_seconds": 136.33,
      "duration_seconds": 1.56,
      "text": "About about three months."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 137.75,
      "end_seconds": 141.41,
      "duration_seconds": 3.66,
      "text": "I'll try to keep this as efficient as I can."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 142.21,
      "end_seconds": 145.63,
      "duration_seconds": 3.42,
      "text": "Thank you, uh, I appreciate it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 146.32,
      "end_seconds": 150.65,
      "duration_seconds": 4.33,
      "text": "Do you have any allergies to medicines, food, anything at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 151.13,
      "end_seconds": 153.2,
      "duration_seconds": 2.07,
      "text": "Yes, I'm allergic to aspirin."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 154.55,
      "end_seconds": 157.29,
      "duration_seconds": 2.74,
      "text": "Let me know if I'm going too fast."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 157.7,
      "end_seconds": 160.01,
      "duration_seconds": 2.31,
      "text": "No, um, you're fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 160.36,
      "end_seconds": 162.58,
      "duration_seconds": 2.22,
      "text": "What about operations, anything like that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 163.3,
      "end_seconds": 166.96,
      "duration_seconds": 3.66,
      "text": "Just a hernia repair, about five years back."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 167.69,
      "end_seconds": 171.73,
      "duration_seconds": 4.04,
      "text": "Is there anything you were hoping to get out of today's visit?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 172.29,
      "end_seconds": 176.3,
      "duration_seconds": 4.01,
      "text": "Mostly I just want to understand what's going on."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 177.29,
      "end_seconds": 184.7,
      "duration_seconds": 7.41,
      "text": "Okay, so the vitals from earlier. BP is 120 over 78, heart rate 77, saturation 99 percent, temperature is 37.0 degrees."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 186.11,
      "end_seconds": 188.67,
      "duration_seconds": 2.56,
      "text": "Thanks. Did you manage to eat before coming?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 190.26,
      "end_seconds": 194.69,
      "duration_seconds": 4.43,
      "text": "Yes, um, I had something small this morning."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 195.96,
      "end_seconds": 200.25,
      "duration_seconds": 4.29,
      "text": "Alright, I'd like to examine you now. Please come over here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 200.9,
      "end_seconds": 201.84,
      "duration_seconds": 0.94,
      "text": "Yes, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 202.81,
      "end_seconds": 206.29,
      "duration_seconds": 3.48,
      "text": "Okay, tell me if anything hurts as I press."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 222.04,
      "end_seconds": 226.39,
      "duration_seconds": 4.35,
      "text": "The big toe joint is red, hot, swollen and extremely tender to touch."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 232.17,
      "end_seconds": 237.52,
      "duration_seconds": 5.35,
      "text": "Okay, you can sit back up. Right, is the room warm enough for you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 240.82,
      "end_seconds": 243.92,
      "duration_seconds": 3.1,
      "text": "It's perfect, you know, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 245.52,
      "end_seconds": 268.0,
      "duration_seconds": 22.48,
      "text": "Okay, so my impression is this: This looks most like an acute gout flare. I want to be honest that this is an impression, not a final answer. I'd also keep pseudogout in mind. Let me just recap so I've got it right. You've had a very painful, swollen big toe, moderate, and no recent illness or rash."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 268.86,
      "end_seconds": 270.41,
      "duration_seconds": 1.55,
      "text": "That's it, yes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 271.82,
      "end_seconds": 275.27,
      "duration_seconds": 3.45,
      "text": "Is it okay if I type while we talk?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 275.69,
      "end_seconds": 278.98,
      "duration_seconds": 3.29,
      "text": "Right, yes, of course, go ahead."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 279.81,
      "end_seconds": 304.7,
      "duration_seconds": 24.89,
      "text": "I'm going to order kidney function tests, for gout. I'd like to arrange a uric acid level for suspected gout. I'll start you on colchicine, 0.5 milligrams, twice a day, for five days. That should help with gout flare. Cut right back on red meat, organ meats, beer and sugary drinks, and drink plenty of water. Avoid taking any extra painkillers on top of what I'm prescribing without checking with us."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 305.93,
      "end_seconds": 319.68,
      "duration_seconds": 13.75,
      "text": "Cut down on salt and fried food for now, it really does make a difference. If the joint gets hotter or you develop a fever, or you feel really unwell, please don't wait, come to the emergency department."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 320.21,
      "end_seconds": 320.91,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Understood."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 321.46,
      "end_seconds": 324.88,
      "duration_seconds": 3.42,
      "text": "I'd like to see you again in a week."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 325.84,
      "end_seconds": 330.06,
      "duration_seconds": 4.22,
      "text": "Sure, I'll make the appointment on the way out."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 331.1,
      "end_seconds": 335.97,
      "duration_seconds": 4.87,
      "text": "Let me check that I've been clear. What will you do once you get home?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 336.78,
      "end_seconds": 345.04,
      "duration_seconds": 8.26,
      "text": "So, I take the colchicine, 0.5 milligrams, twice a day and come back in a week. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 349.27,
      "end_seconds": 355.35,
      "duration_seconds": 6.08,
      "text": "Yes, exactly right. Okay, good. Call the clinic if you need us in the meantime."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 356.71,
      "end_seconds": 361.07,
      "duration_seconds": 4.36,
      "text": "That's all, um, thank you for your time."
    }
  ]
}